    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, with significant weather volatility threatening our core contributors. **Trea Turner** (65.16) remains our strongest play despite a 31% rain risk in his matchup against Scott. As our primary engine for SB\u2014the scarcest category\u2014**Trea Turner** secures the top spot primarily due to his leadoff role (+10%) and historical efficiency against right-handed pitching. **Kyle Schwarber** follows closely (62.23) as a high-upside play; while his platoon efficiency against Scott is slightly negative, his park factor and recent xwOBA metrics justify his placement in the lineup. **Carson Benge** (51.45) rounds out our active participants. While his score is marginal, he benefits from a +7% platoon adjustment against Nola, providing enough situational stability to justify the start, even if we are bracing for the rain that shadows all three players.\n\nThe bench decision for today was relatively straightforward due to off-days for several key assets, including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Christian Yelich**. With these hitters unavailable, we are essentially forced into a thin lineup construction. Other rostered players like **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** are effectively sidelined today as the team navigates this heavy off-day schedule. We are monitoring the weather closely; should the game involving **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Carson Benge** be washed out, our total game caps will remain preserved, allowing us to pivot to a full-strength roster when our premium talent returns from the bench tomorrow.",
